{"book":10,"chapter":13,"rubric":"LEARNING RUST / RUST AFTER PYTHON / CHAPTER 13","slides":[{"title":"Python and Rust classes","sub":"Chapter 13 · struct, impl, trait","short":"Intro","main":"struct — data, impl — methods, trait — behavior; operators are traits too.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["class","struct, impl, trait","Operators are traits"],"captions":["Python: data and behavior in a class, inheritance, __dunder__ methods","Rust: struct — data, impl — methods, trait — shared behavior; no inheritance","Operator overloading is also done with traits from the standard library"],"frames":[[{"t":"cell","id":"pa","x":90.0,"y":60.0,"w":130.0,"h":34.0,"text":"class","tone":"muted","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"pb","x":270.0,"y":60.0,"w":130.0,"h":34.0,"text":"struct + impl","tone":"green","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5}],[{"t":"cell","id":"a0","x":70.0,"y":66.0,"w":90.0,"h":34.0,"text":"struct","tone":"green","size":12.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"a1","x":180.0,"y":66.0,"w":90.0,"h":34.0,"text":"impl","tone":"green","size":12.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"a2","x":290.0,"y":66.0,"w":90.0,"h":34.0,"text":"trait","tone":"green","size":12.0,"sub_size":8.5}],[{"t":"cell","id":"pa","x":90.0,"y":60.0,"w":130.0,"h":34.0,"text":"__add__","tone":"muted","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"pb","x":270.0,"y":60.0,"w":130.0,"h":34.0,"text":"impl Add","tone":"green","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5}]],"cues":[19.6,33.1]}]},{"title":"Class","sub":"new, self, pub","short":"Class","main":"No constructors; three kinds of self; pub opens access.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["__init__ → new","self","pub"],"captions":["No constructors: an instance is a struct literal; by convention you write a new function","The first parameter says what the method does: &self reads, &mut self changes, self takes","Everything is private by default, visible in the module; pub opens access — no underscores"],"frames":[[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["impl User {","    fn new(name: &str) -> User { … }","}"],"hl":[1],"lang":"rust","size":10.5,"lh":24.0,"w":340.0}],[{"t":"cell","id":"a0","x":70.0,"y":66.0,"w":90.0,"h":34.0,"text":"&self","tone":"green","size":11.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"a1","x":180.0,"y":66.0,"w":90.0,"h":34.0,"text":"&mut self","tone":"yellow","size":11.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"a2","x":290.0,"y":66.0,"w":90.0,"h":34.0,"text":"self","tone":"red","size":11.0,"sub_size":8.5}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["pub struct User {","    pub name: String,","    age: u32,   // private","}"],"hl":[1],"lang":"rust","size":10.5,"lh":22.0,"w":340.0}]],"cues":[13.6,28.3]}]},{"title":"Properties and class methods","sub":"Getters and associated functions","short":"Properties","main":"Getters and setters are methods; classmethod is an associated function.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["@property → getter","setter","@classmethod → new"],"captions":["No property attribute: a getter is a plain method fn name(&self) -> &str","A setter is a method with &mut self: fn set_age(&mut self, v: u32)","@classmethod and @staticmethod → associated functions without self: User::new(…), Config::default()"],"frames":[[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["fn name(&self) -> &str {","    &self.name","}"],"hl":[0],"lang":"rust","size":11.0,"lh":24.0,"w":340.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["fn set_age(&mut self, v: u32) {","    self.age = v;","}"],"hl":[0],"lang":"rust","size":11.0,"lh":24.0,"w":340.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":50.0,"lines":["let u = User::new(\"Anya\");","let c = Config::default();"],"lang":"rust","size":12.0,"lh":28.0,"w":340.0}]],"cues":[16.0,30.8]}]},{"title":"Inheritance","sub":"Composition","short":"Inheritance","main":"No inheritance: composition and traits.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["No inheritance","Composition","No diamond"],"captions":["Structs don't inherit fields and methods","A struct holds another in a field and calls its methods; shared behavior goes in a trait","No diamond problem or fragile base class: changing the base breaks no children"],"frames":[[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":90.0,"y":40.0,"w":100.0,"h":28.0,"text":"Animal","tone":"muted","size":11.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b","x":90.0,"y":110.0,"w":100.0,"h":28.0,"text":"Dog","tone":"muted","size":11.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"line","id":"e","x1":90.0,"y1":56.0,"x2":90.0,"y2":96.0,"tone":"muted","arrow":true,"width":1.6},{"t":"text","id":"x","x":270.0,"y":80.0,"text":"✕ in Rust","tone":"red","size":13.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["struct Dog {","    animal: Animal,   // inside","    tricks: u32,","}"],"hl":[1],"lang":"rust","size":11.0,"lh":22.0,"w":340.0}],[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":180.0,"y":60.0,"w":250.0,"h":34.0,"text":"fragile base class → none","tone":"green","size":11.0,"sub_size":8.5}]],"cues":[11.3,30.7]}]},{"title":"Trait","sub":"trait and impl for","short":"Trait","main":"A description of behavior; implementation is separate.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Declaration","Implementation","ABC and Protocol"],"captions":["trait Shape { fn area(&self) -> f64; } — a list of required methods","impl Shape for Circle { … } — written separately, even for a foreign type; the compiler rejects an incomplete one","Python ABC and Protocol are the closest relatives"],"frames":[[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["trait Shape {","    fn area(&self) -> f64;","}"],"hl":[1],"lang":"rust","size":11.5,"lh":24.0,"w":340.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["impl Shape for Circle {","    fn area(&self) -> f64 {","        3.14159 * self.r * self.r","    }","}"],"hl":[0],"lang":"rust","size":9.5,"lh":20.0,"w":340.0}],[{"t":"cell","id":"pa","x":90.0,"y":60.0,"w":130.0,"h":34.0,"text":"ABC / Protocol","tone":"muted","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"pb","x":270.0,"y":60.0,"w":130.0,"h":34.0,"text":"trait","tone":"green","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5}]],"cues":[17.6,24.1]}]},{"title":"Polymorphism","sub":"impl Trait and dyn Trait","short":"Polymorphism","main":"Default methods, static and dynamic dispatch.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Default method","impl Trait","dyn Trait"],"captions":["A method with a body in a trait is implemented “for free”; a type may replace it","Static polymorphism: fn f(s: &impl Shape) — a version per type, fast","Dynamic: Vec<Box<dyn Shape>> — different types in one vector, call via method table"],"frames":[[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["trait Shape {","    fn area(&self) -> f64;","    fn describe(&self) -> String {","        format!(\"{}\", self.area())","    }","}"],"hl":[2,3],"lang":"rust","size":8.5,"lh":18.0,"w":340.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":50.0,"lines":["fn show(s: &impl Shape) {","    println!(\"{}\", s.area());","}"],"hl":[0],"lang":"rust","size":11.0,"lh":26.0,"w":340.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":50.0,"lines":["let v: Vec<Box<dyn Shape>> = vec![","    Box::new(Circle { r: 1.0 }),","    Box::new(Rect { w: 2.0, h: 3.0 }),","];"],"hl":[0],"lang":"rust","size":9.5,"lh":22.0,"w":340.0}]],"cues":[12.3,25.0]}]},{"title":"Display and Debug","sub":"__str__ and __repr__","short":"Display","main":"Display is for people, Debug is for programmers.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["__str__ → Display","__repr__ → Debug","to_string"],"captions":["Display — for the user: impl fmt::Display, written by hand, printed with {}","Debug — for the programmer: #[derive(Debug)], printed with {:?}","Once Display is implemented, to_string() works automatically"],"frames":[[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["impl fmt::Display for P {","    fn fmt(&self, f: &mut fmt::Formatter) -> fmt::Result {","        write!(f, \"({}, {})\", self.x, self.y)","    }","}"],"hl":[0,2],"lang":"rust","size":7.5,"lh":20.0,"w":340.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":50.0,"lines":["#[derive(Debug)]","struct P { x: i32, y: i32 }","println!(\"{:?}\", p);   // P { x: 1, y: 2 }"],"hl":[0],"lang":"rust","size":10.0,"lh":24.0,"w":340.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":50.0,"lines":["let s: String = p.to_string();","// \"(1, 2)\""],"hl":[0],"lang":"rust","size":12.0,"lh":28.0,"w":340.0}]],"cues":[14.8,28.1]}]},{"title":"Comparison","sub":"PartialEq, PartialOrd, Hash","short":"Comparison","main":"derive compares fields in order; Eq and Ord are for total orders.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["__eq__ → PartialEq","__lt__ → PartialOrd","Hash and Eq"],"captions":["#[derive(PartialEq)] — == and != over all fields","#[derive(PartialOrd)] — lexicographic order by fields; custom — partial_cmp by hand","__hash__ → #[derive(Hash)]; Eq and Ord only for types where comparison is always defined (f64 has NaN)"],"frames":[[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":50.0,"lines":["#[derive(PartialEq)]","struct P { x: i32, y: i32 }","p == q"],"hl":[0],"lang":"rust","size":11.0,"lh":24.0,"w":340.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":50.0,"lines":["#[derive(PartialOrd, PartialEq)]","struct V(u32, u32);","V(1, 9) < V(2, 0)   // true"],"hl":[0,2],"lang":"rust","size":10.0,"lh":24.0,"w":340.0}],[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":90.0,"y":60.0,"w":130.0,"h":34.0,"text":"f64: PartialOrd\n(has NaN)","tone":"yellow","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b","x":270.0,"y":60.0,"w":130.0,"h":34.0,"text":"i32: Ord","tone":"green","size":11.0,"sub_size":8.5}]],"cues":[15.2,25.6]}]},{"title":"Operators","sub":"Add and friends","short":"Operators","main":"impl Add, Output, AddAssign, Index.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["__add__ → Add","Output","+= and index"],"captions":["impl Add for V { type Output = V; fn add(self, o: V) -> V { … } } — the + operator for your type","The result type is the associated Output: the dot product of two vectors returns a number","AddAssign for +=, Index and IndexMut for v[i]; Sub, Mul, Div, Rem, Neg are next to it in std::ops"],"frames":[[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":30.0,"lines":["impl Add for V {","    type Output = V;","    fn add(self, o: V) -> V {","        V { x: self.x + o.x, y: self.y + o.y }","    }","}"],"hl":[0,2],"lang":"rust","size":8.5,"lh":18.0,"w":340.0}],[{"t":"cell","id":"pa","x":90.0,"y":60.0,"w":130.0,"h":34.0,"text":"V + V → V","tone":"green","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"pb","x":270.0,"y":60.0,"w":130.0,"h":34.0,"text":"V * V → f64","tone":"yellow","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["impl AddAssign for V { … }   // +=","impl Index<usize> for V { … }   // v[i]"],"lang":"rust","size":9.0,"lh":26.0,"w":340.0}]],"cues":[9.6,27.3]}]},{"title":"Operator details","sub":"References and newtype","short":"Details","main":"Operators for references; coherence; newtype.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["References","Coherence","Newtype"],"captions":["Operators are also implemented for references: &a + &b — no extra copies","You can't implement a foreign trait for a foreign type: two libraries don't conflict","The workaround is a one-field wrapper: struct Meters(f64); — the newtype pattern"],"frames":[[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":50.0,"lines":["impl Add<&V> for &V { … }","let c = &a + &b;   // a and b intact"],"hl":[1],"lang":"rust","size":10.5,"lh":26.0,"w":340.0}],[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":90.0,"y":60.0,"w":130.0,"h":34.0,"text":"foreign trait\n+ foreign type ✕","tone":"red","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b","x":270.0,"y":60.0,"w":130.0,"h":34.0,"text":"own trait\nor own type ✓","tone":"green","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":50.0,"lines":["struct Wrapper(Vec<String>);","impl fmt::Display for Wrapper { … }"],"hl":[0],"lang":"rust","size":10.0,"lh":28.0,"w":340.0}]],"cues":[13.1,31.6]}]},{"title":"Iterator and Drop","sub":"__iter__ and __exit__","short":"Iterator","main":"next() gives for and methods; Drop replaces with.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["__iter__ → Iterator","IntoIterator","__exit__ → Drop"],"captions":["Implement next() — and the type gets for and dozens of ready-made methods","IntoIterator lets you use a type in for by value and by reference","A context manager is replaced by Drop: drop runs when a value leaves scope — no with block"],"frames":[[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["impl Iterator for Count {","    type Item = u32;","    fn next(&mut self) -> Option<u32> { … }","}"],"hl":[2],"lang":"rust","size":9.0,"lh":22.0,"w":340.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":50.0,"lines":["for x in my_collection { … }","for x in &my_collection { … }"],"lang":"rust","size":11.0,"lh":28.0,"w":340.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["impl Drop for File {","    fn drop(&mut self) { /* close */ }","}"],"hl":[1],"lang":"rust","size":10.5,"lh":24.0,"w":340.0}]],"cues":[13.6,33.4]}]},{"title":"dataclass","sub":"derive","short":"derive","main":"Debug, Clone, PartialEq, Default; Clone vs Copy.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["@dataclass → derive","Default","Clone and Copy"],"captions":["@dataclass → #[derive(Debug, Clone, PartialEq)]: printing, copy, and comparison in one line","#[derive(Default)] and User { age: 30, ..Default::default() } — default values","Clone — a deep copy; Copy — copy on assignment, only for simple data"],"frames":[[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":50.0,"lines":["#[derive(Debug, Clone, PartialEq)]","struct User { name: String, age: u32 }"],"hl":[0],"lang":"rust","size":9.5,"lh":28.0,"w":340.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":50.0,"lines":["#[derive(Default)]","let u = User { age: 30, ..Default::default() };"],"hl":[1],"lang":"rust","size":9.0,"lh":28.0,"w":340.0}],[{"t":"cell","id":"pa","x":90.0,"y":60.0,"w":130.0,"h":34.0,"text":"Clone\ndeep copy","tone":"blue","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"pb","x":270.0,"y":60.0,"w":130.0,"h":34.0,"text":"Copy\nsimple only","tone":"green","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5}]],"cues":[13.9,28.9]}]},{"title":"Summary","sub":"What's next","short":"Summary","main":"Next — dictionaries and sets.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Remember","Mapping","Next"],"captions":["class → struct + impl; __init__ → new; property → getter; inheritance → composition and traits","__str__ → Display; __repr__ → Debug; __eq__ → PartialEq; __add__ → Add; __iter__ → Iterator; __exit__ → Drop","Next chapter — Python dicts, HashMap, and sets"],"frames":[[{"t":"cell","id":"a0","x":50.0,"y":66.0,"w":76.0,"h":30.0,"text":"struct","tone":"green","size":10.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"a1","x":136.0,"y":66.0,"w":76.0,"h":30.0,"text":"impl","tone":"green","size":10.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"a2","x":222.0,"y":66.0,"w":76.0,"h":30.0,"text":"trait","tone":"green","size":10.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"a3","x":308.0,"y":66.0,"w":76.0,"h":30.0,"text":"derive","tone":"green","size":10.5,"sub_size":8.5}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":30.0,"lines":["__str__  → Display","__eq__   → PartialEq","__add__  → Add","__iter__ → Iterator"],"lang":"rust","size":11.0,"lh":22.0,"w":340.0}],[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":180.0,"y":60.0,"w":250.0,"h":34.0,"text":"dict ↔ HashMap · set ↔ HashSet","tone":"blue","size":10.5,"sub_size":8.5}]],"cues":[13.1,28.7]}]}]}